KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp26
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ the spliced type is int: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Static reflection (P2996R13, adopted for C++26 after N5008): ^^int is a
reflection of int, and [: r :] splices it back as a type.  CBMC reports a
parse error at ^^.  Checked with GCC 16 -freflection; header-free (it
needs no <meta>).
